	<h3>ACT IV - THE KNIGHT OF GOD</h3>
	<p>
		Slowly, the Lunarians began to take control of America, not only by
		creating “vessels for the king's essence”, but also by attacking the
		human culture, starting with language. No one understood their own
		thoughts, so they had to accept the Lunarian culture by force in order
		to survive. However, in the midst of all this storm, a familiar voice
		returned to bring faith to the human race... Alice Avenue broadcasted
		over the radio the story of the Last Son.
	</p>
	<p>
		The Last Son was a young man like you and me, with parents who were
		cutthroats and classmates who were worse. The boy was always alone when
		he went to school, and always in those moments driving towards his
		destiny, he doubted his role in the universe; he always thought that he
		had to help everyone around him, and that he had to win at any cost. One
		day in the midst of his thoughts, the young man was involved in a car
		crash; still b enough to move, he got out of his car and approached the
		dying man with whom he had collided, a familiar face from another
		universe... <b>James Dean</b>.
	</p>
	<p>
		“You won, little bastard... you won...”, this were the last words of the
		man who in this universe, lost. The Last Son was devastated and could
		not hold back his tears, and from the pain and exhaustion caused by the
		accident, he fainted. He woke up in a strange dream, where he found
		himself on a cliff with a vehicle behind him, which was driving at high
		speed. He, to avoid the impact, jumped into the void, and began to
		believe more and more that he could fly, that he could beat death... he
		did it. The young man began to fly high, faster than an airplane. It was
		right here that he woke up and flew as far away as possible from the
		scene of the accident. He kept on believing, and kept on winning at any
		cost in order to save everyone.
	</p>
	<p>
		Alice not only prayed that the Crescent King would remember the hero he
		was before America captured him, she also hoped that the Knight would
		return to save us all again. He listened to her words and executed a
		desperate plan to make the humanity of the Last Son wake up again: throw
		Alice off the top of the Chrysler Building hoping that he would rescue
		her... <b>that never happened</b>.
	</p>
	<blockquote>
		<img
		src="../../../images/data/avenuefall_dark.png"
		class="logo toggleable"
		/>
		<p>Alice Avenue last moments of life.</p>
	</blockquote>
	<p>
		After the Knight's plan failed in every way, the Lunarians continued
		their invasion, brainwashing and altering human brains in major cities
		such as New York. It's at this point that the Knight would compose a
		message apologizing for what happened to Alice, and that she was still
		alive...
	</p>
	<p style="text-align: center;">
		<a href={localizePath("data/monument-mythos")}
		>IN MY WURLD, STATUUES HELLD SOLES</a
		>
	</p>
	<p>
		Something still left the Knight unsatisfied, something made him feel
		hollow, so to try to redeem himself he removed the head of the Alice
		Avenue memorial statue and wear it as if it were his old helmet; even
		though he had only worn it for a day something in him changed, the only
		thing that could be seen was his eye, full of anger... <b
		><i>Grief can make you a monster</i></b
		>.
	</p>
	<h3>ACT V - GOD</h3>
	<p>
		This precise moment is where Apollo 11 comes back to play a vital role,
		so we'll have to go back in time a bit, and put ourselves in Ed Dwight's
		spacesuit again. His body was found on the moon, and it was determined
		that his death was caused by his own weapon; next to him was a tape
		which would be referred to as “THE MOON GOD”. On this tape is revealed
		the conversation Ed had with that someone special who has been hidden
		for quite some time, the God behind the beings that are causing so much
		damage right now... <b>Richard Nixon</b>.
	</p>
	<blockquote>
		<p style="font-size: 0.7rem; font-style: normal;">
			Note: The following audio does not feature the voice of Ed Dwight.
		</p>
		<Tape audio="../../../audio/the_moon_god.mp3" client:only />
		<blockquote>
			<img
				src="../../../images/data/god_dark.png"
				class="logo toggleable"
			/>
			<p>“PHOTOGRAPH OF GOD”<br />by Ed Dwight</p>
		</blockquote>
	</blockquote>
	<p>
		Nixon explains in this tape that he managed to escape from the Horned
		Serpent during the Great Division, and that he ended up on the moon of
		this new universe. He had doubts about whether people would accept him,
		so he created three extensions of himself to run a little experiment,
		which is how The Son, The Knight and The Queen were born. All three went
		somewhat insane, and Nixon concluded that he couldn't risk entering an
		unfriendly planet. Besides, he already knew that the Son would become
		King of the Lunarians, and that if he didn't stop it, he would become
		exceedingly powerful.
	</p>
	<p style="text-align: center;">
		I am sorry, Mr Dwight. No human was ever meant to hear what I have said.
	</p>
	<p>
		Back on our planet, the Queen of the Lunarians tries to talk to the
		Knight telepathically, trying to convince him to leave Earth and join
		the kingdom as Prince, to bring a place of harmony, to repair the peace
		equation, so that he can return to his old self. However, the Knight,
		amidst all the anger he has, still fulfils the words of Alice Avenue:
		“At all times, in all places, the Knight can SAVE US”, and unleashes a
		final attack that would not only destroy him, the Queen and the
		Lunarians, but also restore human culture within 9 months: <b
			>ALCATRAZ CHECKMATE</b
		>.
	</p>
	<p>
		However, there is still the King, who has finally become aware of all he
		has done, and breaks down in tears once again. Grief made him a monster,
		he will not stop crying, he does not want to live, but in that instant,
		he mutates again, assimilating a very familiar form to the Knight's
		helmet, becoming what Nixon feared he would become... <b
			><u>THE HORNED SERPENT LIVES</u></b
		>.
	</p>
	<blockquote>
		<img
			src="../../../images/data/thehornedserpentlives_dark.png"
			class="logo toggleable"
		/>
		<p
			style="font-family: 'VCR'; font-style: normal; text-decoration: underline; font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--blood);"
		>
			THE HORNED SERPENT LIVES.
		</p>
	</blockquote>
	<p>
		Nixon must act fast, he can't let it all end like his own world ended,
		so he decided to render the King, the Knight, the Queen, and himself as
		fiction, so no one will believe in the Crescent King and so he loses his
		powers. That's how this whole world became a comic book called “The
		Nixonverse”, with an endearing story made by a certain “Mister
		Manticore” and beautiful illustrations made by... <b>Ed Dwight?</b>
	</p>
	<p>
		Compared to Nixon, Ed Dwight was twice the God he was, Nixon was just
		one of many survivors who erased the past, to run from the present. Ed
		was everything Nixon wasn't, someone bold, kind and good. He never went
		to the moon, let alone talked to a God, he is today in our world
		creating monuments... <i>Ed Dwight preserves the past.</i>
	</p>
